WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.259
Custody Folio helps parents organize custody notes and supporting files for an attorney

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:08.185
meeting or custody proceeding.

00:00:08.185 --> 00:00:09.629
Remove the emotion.

00:00:09.629 --> 00:00:11.073
Track the data.

00:00:11.073 --> 00:00:14.925
This walkthrough uses fictional examples and synthetic narration.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.886
Start with one dated record.

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:21.258
Add what happened and keep the supporting details with it.

00:00:21.258 --> 00:00:24.630
You do not need an account for the other parent.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.013
Home also gives you a direct route to building a PDF or sharing

00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:30.025
with an attorney.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.679
The timeline brings dated entries together.

00:00:33.679 --> 00:00:38.618
Open Options to choose the date range, filter the kinds of records you

00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:42.037
want to review, and check the details before exporting.

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:46.975
The purpose is to make your own records easier to find and follow.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.346
Here is an actual sample PDF export.

00:00:51.346 --> 00:00:57.189
Notice the factual description: scheduled pickup at six, actual pickup at six fifteen.

00:00:57.189 --> 00:01:01.234
Compare every report with the original records before sharing.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:07.077
A report organizes what you entered; it does not verify an allegation or

00:01:07.077 --> 00:01:08.425
guarantee court acceptance.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:15.108
The picture to PDF builder lets you select screenshots and arrange them into

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.333
a printable document.

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:21.642
Add a neutral title and description, review the page order, and keep the

00:01:21.642 --> 00:01:23.275
original pictures for reference.

00:01:23.275 --> 00:01:26.950
This is the starting screen before selecting any images.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.026
Attorney access is optional.

00:01:30.026 --> 00:01:35.960
Choose a case and authorize sharing, enter the attorney’s exact email, and send

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.243
the private invitation link yourself.

00:01:38.243 --> 00:01:42.351
The attorney verifies that mailbox with a one-time code.

00:01:42.351 --> 00:01:45.090
Access is read-only, with downloads available.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:50.568
You can revoke future access, but you cannot recall copies already downloaded.

00:01:50.568 --> 00:01:52.850
Sharing does not establish representation.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.105
This is the starting point for Custody Folio.

00:01:57.105 --> 00:02:01.827
The core tools are available now, and feedback will help guide what improves

00:02:01.827 --> 00:02:03.280
and what comes next.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.548
What takes the most time when you organize records?

00:02:06.548 --> 00:02:09.454
What would make a report easier to review?

00:02:09.454 --> 00:02:14.175
You can give feedback using a fictional example without sharing personal case details.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:20.889
Visit custody folio dot com to try the web app free for thirty

00:02:20.889 --> 00:02:23.000
days, with no card required.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.489
Web access is five dollars and ninety-nine cents monthly, or fifty-nine dollars and

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:29.756
ninety-nine cents annually.

00:02:29.756 --> 00:02:34.400
Custody Folio helps organize records and does not provide legal advice.
